<title>PHILIPPINES: Asian Dev Bank approves $80 mln loan to Indonesia.</title>
<headline>Asian Dev Bank approves $80 mln loan to Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank said on Thursday it approved a $80-million loan to Indonesia to upgrade infrastructure in 13 fast-growing cities and towns.</p>
<p>The project area includes metropolitan Bogor, Tangerang and Bekasi, areas which have high population growth rates.</p>
<p>The loan, representing a third of the total project cost of $228 million, will be repaid in 25 years, including a grace period of five years.</p>
<p>Interest on the loan will be based on the bank's pool-based variable lending rate system for U.S. dollar loans which is currently at 6.82 percent, the ADB said.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
